    for ($i = 0; $i < $size - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 0; $j < $size - $i - 1; $j++) {
            if (($order == 'ASC' && $set[$j]['age'] > $set[$j+1]['age']) || ($order == 'DESC' && $set[$j]['age'] < $set[$j+1]['age'])) {
                $temp = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $set[$j+1];
                $set[$j+1] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }
    return $set;
}
```

This function takes an associative array called `$set` as its first argument and an optional string parameter called `$order` which determines the sorting order (default is ascending). It sorts the elements in the array using simple switching of elements based on their age value.

You can use this function as follows:

```php
$mySet = array(
    array('name' => 'Alice', 'address' => 'New York', 'age' => 25),
    array('name' => 'Bob', 'address' => 'Chicago', 'age' => 30),
    array('name' => 'Charlie', 'address' => 'Los Angeles', 'age' => 28)
);

// Sort in ascending order
$ascendingOrder = smart_sort_array($mySet);
print_r($ascendingOrder);

// Sort in descending order
$descendingOrder = smart_sort_array($mySet, 'DESC');
print_r($descendingOrder);
```

