2. Use the useCallback hook instead of defining functions inside event handlers to optimize re-rendering.
3. Combine multiple state variables into one state object to reduce the number of setState calls. For example, combine `[selectedTargetPrompt, setSelectedTargetPrompt]` and `[editedName, setEditedName]` into one state object like `[{ selectedTargetPrompt, editedName }, setState]`.
4. Use useCombinedRefs instead of using refs for multiple DOM elements if they share similar functionality.
5. Use useEffect with an empty dependency array to run side effects only once on mounting and unmounting components.
